  "description_html": "Dinosaurs size comparison.\n<p><i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Argentinosaurus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Argentinosaurus\">Argentinosaurus</a></i> (green): 35-36 meters, \n<i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Apatosaurus\" title=\"Apatosaurus\">Apatosaurus</a></i> (blue): 29-30 meters, \n<i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Triceratops\" title=\"Triceratops\">Triceratops</a></i> (orange): 8-9 meters,\nHuman (black): 1.8-2 meters (height).\n</p><p>Based on the latest fossils record (2015) and the following figures from Wikipedia:\n<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Argentinosaurus_scale.png\" title=\"File:Argentinosaurus scale.png\">File:Argentinosaurus_scale.png</a> by Matt Martyniuk,\n<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Human-triceratops_size_comparison.svg\" title=\"File:Human-triceratops size comparison.svg\">File:Human-triceratops_size_comparison.svg</a> by Nobu Tamura\nand Matt Wedel's Apatosaurus Sideshow sculpture as basis to the blue silhouette.\n</p>\nZachi Evenor (CC-BY-SA)",
